      "purpose": "`math` is an immutable arbitrary-precision numeric foundation for Go. It provides distinct APIs for signed integers, exact rationals, finite base-10 decimals, and explicitly inexact binary floats. Use ordinary Go numeric types when their fixed width and machine arithmetic are sufficient.",
